B.biX=new A.a4(B.a2i,["A peaceful shoaling fish. It feels best in a group of at least six specimens.","A sociable bottom-dwelling fish that needs soft, non-abrasive substrate.","A hardy freshwater shrimp prized for its activity and vivid colors.","A slow-growing epiphytic plant that tolerates lower light levels.","A versatile moss that provides shelter for fry and shrimp.","A large cichlid that requires a tall tank and a carefully planned stock.","An active, easy-to-breed livebearer. Males are colorful and the species breeds quickly.","A peaceful livebearer that likes harder, slightly alkaline water and room to swim.","A gentle shoaling fish. In a group it shows natural behavior and vivid coloring.","A small algae-eating catfish that needs a mature tank, constant food access, and a group.","A striking labyrinth fish. Males are territorial, so tankmates must be chosen carefully.","A demanding schooling fish needing high temperature, stable parameters, and a large tank.","An active algae eater that grows quite large. Needs swimming space and hiding spots.","A peaceful labyrinth fish that likes floating plants and gentle water movement.","A tiny, peaceful shoaling fish with orange coloring, ideal for small tanks.","A colorful dwarf cichlid that requires clean, stable, warm water and calm tankmates.","A fast-growing stem plant that helps consume nutrients and oxygenate the water.","An impressive rosette plant that needs a nutrient-rich substrate and room for broad leaves.","A hardy epiphytic plant attached to roots or rocks instead of being planted in substrate.","An undemanding foreground/midground plant. It may shed leaves after replanting.","A colorful stem plant. Stronger light and regular trimming bring out red leaves.","A decorative stem plant with delicate leaves, requiring good light and nutrients.","An effective algae-eating shrimp. Needs a safe tank without predatory fish.","A predatory snail that helps control other snail populations. Needs hard water for its shell.","A peaceful snail with a distinctive shell that eats algae and does not overbreed in fresh water.","A peaceful shoaling fish with an intense red stripe. Needs a shaded tank and a group.","A gentle shoaling fish with a contrasting black stripe, best kept in a large group.","A small, peaceful rasbora with copper coloring. Needs soft water and plant cover.","A larger livebearer with a tall dorsal fin. Likes hard, alkaline water and a spacious tank.","An active livebearer whose males have a characteristic elongated tail fin.","A hardy, peaceful livebearer. Does well in a group with more females than males.","An active tetra with a bluish sheen. Needs swimming space and a shoal.","A shoaling fish with a red nose whose intensity indicates good health.","A peaceful shoaling fish. Males display fins in gentle territorial shows.","A colorful harem dwarf cichlid. Needs hiding spots, calm tankmates, and stable water.","A gentle, strikingly colored gourami that needs a calm tank with floating plants.","A small labyrinth fish. Needs a calm water surface, plants, and gentle current.","A sociable bottom-dwelling cory. Keep in a group and provide fine, safe sand.","A hardy bottom fish with a spotted pattern. Does best in a group on soft substrate.","A miniature cory that sometimes swims mid-water. Requires a large group.","A nocturnal pleco needing driftwood, hiding spots, and plant-based food. Grows quite large.","A nocturnal, eel-like loach. Provide fine sand, hiding spots, and a group of several.","An active bottom fish requiring well-oxygenated water, rocks, and swimming space.","A large, very active shoaling danio. Needs a long, covered tank.","A hardy and very lively shoaling fish. Needs a lid and room for fast swimming.","A tiny fish with pearly spots. Needs a densely planted tank and a calm shoal.","A territorial cichlid that needs a large tank, hiding spots, and careful tankmate selection.","A small Lake Tanganyika cichlid that lives in shells. Needs hard, alkaline water.","A skittish surface fish with an unusual shape. Needs a lid and a calm tank.","A large, active shoaling rainbowfish. Needs a long tank and strong lighting.","An energetic barb that should be kept in a larger group to reduce fin-nipping.","A hardy, active shoaling barb. Needs cooler water and plenty of swimming space.","A low, slow-growing epiphytic plant. Do not bury the rhizome and avoid strong light.","A branching moss that attaches to roots and rocks. Needs regular trimming.","An easy plant with long leaves, forming a green wall in the tank background.","A stem plant that can turn pink or red with good light and fertilization.","A fast-growing stem plant with feathery leaves, good for beginner aquarists.","A slower-growing, aromatic stem plant with fleshy leaves. Tolerates moderate light well.","A low carpeting plant. Needs strong light, nutrient access, and patient rooting.","A tiny plant forming a low carpet. Grows best with strong light, CO2, and regular fertilization.","A floating plant providing shade and absorbing nutrients from the water. Control its fast growth.","A hardy rootless plant that can float or be weighted in substrate. Absorbs nitrates well.","A small floating plant that provides shade. Thin out clusters regularly to keep gas exchange open.","A rosette plant with broad leaves that grows well in nutrient-rich substrate and moderate light.","A yellow variant of the Neocaridina shrimp. Provide moss, biofilm, stable parameters, and no predators.","A blue Neocaridina variant that needs a mature tank, hiding spots, and regular feeding.","A delicate shrimp requiring soft, acidic water, active substrate, and very stable parameters.","A large algae-eating snail with a dark shell. Needs hard water and natural surface food.","A useful snail that eats leftovers and algae. Its numbers depend on available food.","A nocturnal snail that burrows through substrate. Aerates sand but overbreeds with excess food.","A small, vividly colored crayfish. Provide plenty of hiding spots and avoid delicate shrimp tankmates.","A large shrimp that filters water with its fan-like appendages. Needs strong but safe flow and fine food.","A peaceful, small livebearer with very vivid colors.","A small shoaling fish with a semi-transparent, red body.","An ideal fish for nano tanks and shrimp tanks.","A hardy fish that prefers somewhat cooler water.","A gentler and hardier relative of the popular Ram cichlid.","A small species related to the dwarf gourami with warm coloring.","A fast-growing floating plant that pulls nitrates out of the water.","A stunning plant with large, red-brown leaves.","A tall background plant with long, ribbon-like leaves.","A large, non-aggressive shrimp that catches food from the water flow.","A large, striking snail from Sulawesi with vividly colored body.","A small snail with horn-like protrusions on its shell, great at eating algae.","An unusual fish with an elongated, trunk-like snout.","A small shoaling fish similar to the harlequin rasbora with an orange stripe.","A fast-growing submerged plant producing a lot of oxygen.","A striking stem plant with intensely red leaves under strong light."],t.w)
